{
  "sn12.31:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.31 ",
  "sn12.31:0.2": "4. Kaḷāra the Aristocrat ",
  "sn12.31:0.3": "What Has Come to Be ",
  "sn12.31:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.31:1.2": "Then the Buddha said to Venerable Sāriputta, ",
  "sn12.31:1.3": "“Sāriputta, this was said in ‘The Way to the Far Shore’, in ‘The Questions of Ajita’: ",
  "sn12.31:2.1": "‘There are those who have appraised the teaching, ",
  "sn12.31:2.2": "and many kinds of trainees here. ",
  "sn12.31:2.3": "Now you, being alert, are asked ",
  "sn12.31:2.4": "to tell me their behavior, good fellow.’ ",
  "sn12.31:3.1": "How should we see the detailed meaning of this brief statement?” ",
  "sn12.31:3.2": "When he said this, Sāriputta kept silent. ",
  "sn12.31:4.1": "For a second time … ",
  "sn12.31:4.2": "",
  "sn12.31:4.3": "For a third time … ",
  "sn12.31:4.4": "",
  "sn12.31:5.1": "",
  "sn12.31:5.2": "",
  "sn12.31:5.3": "",
  "sn12.31:5.4": "",
  "sn12.31:6.1": "",
  "sn12.31:6.2": "Sāriputta kept silent. ",
  "sn12.31:7.1": "“Sāriputta, do you see that this has come to be?” ",
  "sn12.31:7.2": "“Sir, one truly sees with right wisdom that this has come to be. ",
  "sn12.31:7.3": "Seeing this, one is practicing for disillusionment, dispassion, and cessation regarding what has come to be. ",
  "sn12.31:7.4": "One truly sees with right wisdom that it came to be with that as fuel. ",
  "sn12.31:7.5": "Seeing this, one is practicing for disillusionment, dispassion, 